+{"timestamp_utc":"2026-08-30T10:36:00Z","branch":"direct_bezout_selectors","note":"Self-contained proof architecture: first prove Bezout by least positive integer linear combination. For each ordered pair i != j choose r_ij m_j+s_ij m_i=1; define N_i=product_{j!=i}m_j, c_i=product_{j!=i}r_ij, e_i=c_iN_i. Then e_i=1 mod m_i and 0 mod all other moduli, so x=sum a_i e_i works. For uniqueness, if all m_i divide n, induct on Q_r=product_{i<=r}m_i. Multiplying pairwise Bezout identities between m_{r+1} and m_j (j<=r) gives A Q_r+B m_{r+1}=1; from n=Q_rt and m_{r+1}|n infer m_{r+1}|t, hence Q_{r+1}|n."}
